---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy — OpenLearn AI"
  description="The short version: this site currently collects nothing. No cookies, no analytics, no trackers. Your progress lives in your browser's local storage.">
  <section class="container prose" style="padding-block:var(--sp-12);">
    <h1 style="font-size:var(--fs-500);">Privacy</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--c-ink-soft);">Version 0.1 · public preview · last updated 2026-07-09</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p><strong>This site currently collects no personal data at all.</strong>
    No cookies, no analytics, no trackers, no third-party scripts.</p>

    <h2>Where your progress lives</h2>
    <p>Your lessons, XP, streaks, badges, and flashcard schedule are stored in
    your browser's <em>local storage</em>, on your device. We can't see them.
    Clearing your browser data deletes them; that is entirely in your hands.
    "Make available offline" stores lesson copies in your browser's cache the
    same way.</p>

    <h2>When accounts arrive</h2>
    <p>An optional sign-in (for syncing progress across devices) is planned.
    When it launches, this page will change <em>before</em> the feature does,
    and it will follow the same rules we've committed to publicly: minimal
    data, no selling, no ad networks, easy export and deletion.</p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is served by a content delivery network, which processes IP
    addresses transiently to deliver pages and protect against abuse, as all
    web hosting does. We run no server-side logging of our own.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or concerns: open an issue on the project repository —
    everything about this project happens in the open.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
